## Derived -- do not edit
## Canonical certificate paths. The installer recomputes most of these
## every run, so editing one here moves nothing.
##
## The exceptions are PKI_web_vhost_cert, PKI_web_vhost_key,
## PKI_web_trust_chain, PKI_client_encrypt_cert and
## PKI_client_encrypt_key. To serve or use a certificate FOG did not
## issue you may either leave those alone and make each path resolve to
## your file (a symlink is enough), or set them to where your files
## really are -- the installer only resets one of them while it still
## holds a default of its own. Either way FOG stops re-issuing it.
##
## The two client_encrypt keys are the fog-client communication keypair,
## normally set with --client-cert/--client-key. Relocating them is a
## re-pin event if the material differs: the installer says so, and the
## key must stay readable by the web server or no client can
## authenticate.
##
## Simplest of all: drop web-leaf.pem and web-leaf.key into
## PKI_custom_dir above and re-run the installer, which finds the pair
## and points these at it for you.
PKI_root_ca_cert='/opt/fog/snapins/ssl/CA/.fogCA.pem'
PKI_root_ca_key='/etc/fog/pki/root/ca/.fogCA.key'
PKI_web_ca_cert='/etc/fog/pki/web/ca/.fogWebCA.pem'
PKI_web_ca_key='/etc/fog/pki/web/ca/.fogWebCA.key'
PKI_web_external_root_cert=''
PKI_web_trust_chain='/etc/fog/pki/web/ca/.fogWebCAchain.pem'
PKI_web_vhost_cert='/etc/fog/pki/web/leaf/.webLeaf.pem'
PKI_web_vhost_key='/etc/fog/pki/web/leaf/.webLeaf.key'
PKI_client_encrypt_cert='/etc/fog/pki/client/leaf/.srvpublic.crt'
PKI_client_encrypt_key='/etc/fog/pki/client/leaf/.srvprivate.key'
PKI_sb_ca_cert='/etc/fog/pki/secureboot/ca/.fogSBCA.pem'
PKI_sb_codesign_cert='/etc/fog/pki/secureboot/leaf/sign.pem'
PKI_sb_codesign_key='/etc/fog/pki/secureboot/leaf/sign.key'
